//RS /// The rollback path only does real work when the tree has a state adapter.
//RS /// With no adapter, `prepare_rollback` returns early and `restore_rollback`
//RS /// never touches the store, so a rollback test on a bare tree proves nothing
//RS /// about the durable body. This sets an adapter first, so the upgrade really
//RS /// copies the store aside and the rollback reads it back.
